usage: ugit <command> [<args>]

  init                    create an empty repository in .ugit
  add <path>...           stage files (a directory stages all below it)
  commit -m <message>     record the staged tree
  status                  show staged, unstaged and untracked changes
  diff [--cached] [<rev> [<rev>]]
                          show changes as a unified diff
  log [--oneline] [<rev>] show history
  show [<rev>]            show a commit and its changes
  branch [<name> [<rev>]] list branches, or create one
  tag [<name> [<rev>]]    list tags, or create one
  checkout [-b] <rev>     switch branches, or detach HEAD at a commit
  checkout -- <path>...   restore files from the index
  merge <rev>             merge another line of history into HEAD
  reset [--hard] <rev>    move the branch, resetting the index (and files)

plumbing: hash-object, cat-file, write-tree, rev-parse, merge-base
